 "input": "buying a flat, what our solicitor said happens. offer accepted through the estate agent. solicitor sends client care letter, ID and source of funds checks (anti money laundering). seller's solicitor sends the draft contract and property info forms. our solicitor orders searches (local authority, water, environmental) and raises enquiries. mortgage lender does its valuation and issues the mortgage offer, solicitor also acts for the lender. survey is our job, separate. once searches back and enquiries answered, report on title, we sign the contract, pay deposit, exchange contracts, completion date fixed. on completion lender sends funds, solicitor pays stamp duty and registers us at Land Registry.",
